Import fixtures for the engine tests.

- `*.csv`: hand-written excerpts that follow the published layouts of each bank's or QuickBooks' CSV download (title and summary blocks, header names, sign conventions, group and total rows). Names and amounts are invented.
- `ofxparse-bank_medium.ofx`: real OFX 1.02 test file from the ofxparse project (https://github.com/jseutter/ofxparse, tests/fixtures), MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2009 Jerry Seutter.
- `two-accounts-sgml.ofx`, `two-accounts-xml.ofx`: hand-written, synthetic two-account downloads (an OFX 1.02 SGML file and an OFX 2.2 XML file) laid out as in OFX specification sections 11.3.1 (BANKACCTFROM), 11.4.2.2 (STMTRS, BANKTRANLIST, LEDGERBAL) and 11.4.3 (STMTTRN, including BANKACCTTO) as cited by the open-source ofxtools models (https://github.com/csingley/ofxtools/blob/master/ofxtools/models/bank/stmt.py), and as in the ofxparse fixture above. Account numbers, names and amounts are invented. The two accounts in the SGML file deliberately reuse the same FITID values.
